---
// @ts-nocheck
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="API Docs"
  description="Reference for the UptimeCove HTTP API: monitors, checks, status pages, incidents, maintenance windows, notification channels, badges and authentication."
  heading="API Documentation"
  ogType="article"
>
  <p>Base URL is your own deployment's origin — <code>https://uptimecove.com</code> is used below as an example.</p>

  <div class="mt-8 space-y-6">
      <section class="card p-6">
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-blue-600">GET /api/status/&lbrace;slug&rbrace;</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Public. Returns status page and monitors with daily uptime. <span class="font-mono text-xs bg-slate-100 px-1 rounded">Cache-Control: no-store</span></p>
        <pre class="mt-3 overflow-auto rounded-xl bg-slate-900 p-4 text-xs text-slate-300"><code>&lbrace;
  "page": "default",
  "monitors": [&lbrace; "id": 1, "name": "API", "status": "up", "dailyUptime": [...] &rbrace;]
&rbrace;</code></pre>
      </section>

      <section class="card p-6">
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-blue-600">POST /api/monitors</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Auth required. Create monitor. Body: <code>name, url, method?, expected_status?, interval_seconds?, timeout_ms?, body_must_contain?, body_must_not_contain?, max_response_time_ms?, custom_headers? (JSON)</code></p>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">Form posts redirect to /dashboard, JSON returns 201.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="card p-6">
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-blue-600">PUT /api/monitors/&lbrace;id&rbrace;</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Update monitor. Same fields as create, partial allowed.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="card p-6">
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-blue-600">POST /api/monitors/&lbrace;id&rbrace;/toggle · POST /api/monitors/&lbrace;id&rbrace;/delete</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Pause/resume or delete. Returns 204 or 404.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="card p-6">
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-blue-600">POST /api/checks/run</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Auth required. Forces checked batch for due monitors. Returns <code>&lbrace; checked, failed &rbrace;</code></p>
      </section>

      <section class="card p-6">
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-blue-600">GET /api/status-pages · POST /api/status-pages</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">List/create status pages. Fields: title, slug, description, branding_logo_url, branding_theme, custom_domain, is_public</p>
      </section>

      <section class="card p-6">
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-blue-600">PUT /api/status-pages/&lbrace;id&rbrace; · DELETE /api/status-pages/&lbrace;id&rbrace;</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Update/delete page. Default page protected if sole page.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="card p-6">
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-blue-600">PUT /api/status-pages/&lbrace;id&rbrace;/monitors</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Set ordered monitor ids: <code>&lbrace; monitorIds: [1,2] &rbrace;</code></p>
      </section>

      <section class="card p-6">
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-blue-600">GET /api/notification-channels · POST /api/notification-channels</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Types: email, webhook, slack, discord. Config: url/webhook_url, to, endpoint etc.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="card p-6">
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-blue-600">POST /api/incidents/&lbrace;id&rbrace;/resolve · POST /api/incidents/&lbrace;id&rbrace;/updates</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Resolve incident or add timeline update (message, author).</p>
      </section>

      <section class="card p-6">
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-blue-600">POST /api/maintenance · DELETE /api/maintenance/&lbrace;id&rbrace;</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Maintenance windows to suppress alerts. Fields: title, monitor_id (null=global), start_at, end_at (unix sec or ISO), description.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="card p-6">
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-blue-600">GET /api/badge/&lbrace;slug&rbrace;</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Public. Returns an SVG uptime/status badge for a public status page — embeddable straight into a README. Query params: <code>label</code>, <code>style</code>.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="card p-6">
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-blue-600">POST /api/heartbeat/&lbrace;id&rbrace;/ping · GET /api/heartbeat/&lbrace;id&rbrace;/ping</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Public (the URL is the secret). Dead-man's-switch endpoint for cron jobs and backups: <code>id</code> is the monitor id, and each ping marks the monitor up and resolves any open incident. If no ping arrives within <code>grace_seconds</code>, the scheduled worker marks it down. GET is accepted so <code>curl</code> in a crontab works without flags.</p>
        <pre class="mt-3 overflow-auto rounded-xl bg-slate-900 p-4 text-xs text-slate-300"><code>curl -fsS https://uptimecove.example/api/heartbeat/7/ping</code></pre>
      </section>

      <section class="card p-6">
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Auth</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">Single admin token via <code>ADMIN_TOKEN</code>. Login POSTs to <code>/api/auth/login</code> and sets a <code>uc_session</code> HttpOnly cookie (7d, Secure in prod, SameSite=Lax). Machine clients can send <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;api key&gt;</code> instead. Everything under <code>/dashboard</code> and <code>/api/*</code> requires auth <em>except</em> <code>/api/auth/*</code>, <code>/api/status/*</code>, <code>/api/badge/*</code> and <code>/api/heartbeat/*/ping</code>. The sessions table validates each request, so rotating <code>ADMIN_TOKEN</code> revokes existing sessions.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

  <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-slate-400">
    Found a gap? <a href="https://github.com/iharshalp/UptimeCove/issues/new/choose" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Open an issue</a> or send a PR — undocumented behaviour counts as a bug.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
